<h2>AI ticket enhancement</h2>
<%= javascript_include_tag 'settings', plugin: 'redmine_ai_integration', defer: true %>
<%= form_tag ai_settings_path, id: 'ai-settings-form' do %>
  <div class="box tabular">
    <p><%= label_tag 'settings_enabled', 'Enabled' %><%= hidden_field_tag 'settings[enabled]', '0' %><%= check_box_tag 'settings[enabled]', '1', @settings['enabled'] == '1' %></p>
    <p><%= label_tag :api_key, 'OpenAI API key' %><%= password_field_tag :api_key, '', autocomplete: 'new-password', size: 55 %><br>
      <em>Blank retains the encrypted key. <%= link_to 'Create an OpenAI API key', 'https://platform.openai.com/api-keys', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer' %>. API billing is separate from ChatGPT.</em></p>
    <p><%= label_tag :clear_api_key, 'Remove saved key' %><%= check_box_tag :clear_api_key, '1' %></p>
    <p><%= label_tag 'settings_model', 'Model' %><%= select_tag 'settings[model]', options_for_select(@models, @settings['model']) %><br>
      <em>Save the key first, then Refresh models. Choose a model supporting Responses and structured output.</em></p>
    <p><%= label_tag 'settings_reasoning_effort', 'Reasoning effort' %><%= select_tag 'settings[reasoning_effort]', options_for_select(RedmineAi::Configuration::REASONING_EFFORT_OPTIONS, @settings['reasoning_effort']) %><br>
      <em>Model default preserves the model's normal behavior. Light / Medium / High / Extra High / Ultra map to low / medium / high / xhigh / max. Supported levels depend on the model; higher levels can increase time and token cost.</em></p>
  </div>
  <h3>Code with AI access</h3>
  <p><%= label_tag 'settings_code_role_ids', 'Allowed member roles' %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag 'settings[code_role_ids][]', '' %>
    <%= select_tag 'settings[code_role_ids][]', options_for_select(@code_roles || [], @settings['code_role_ids']), multiple: true, size: 5 %></p>
  <p>Only the selected project roles and administrators can generate/apply code proposals. Existing ticket visibility/edit permissions still apply. Also enable Allow reviewed code changes on each approved Code folder. No role is selected by default.</p>
  <h3>Technical sources</h3>
  <p>Choose server-side code/document folders or database connections. Assign each source to the projects allowed to use its excerpts.</p>
  <%= hidden_field_tag :sources_present, '1' %>
  <div id="ai-source-rows">
    <% @sources.each_with_index do |source, index| %>
      <%= render partial: 'ai_settings/source', locals: {source: source, index: index} %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <p><button type="button" id="ai-add-source">Add technical source</button></p>
  <template id="ai-source-template"><%= render partial: 'ai_settings/source', locals: {source: {}, index: '__SOURCE__'} %></template>
  <p><%= submit_tag 'Save configuration' %></p>
<% end %>
<h3>Connection and source checks</h3>
<p>Save first. Test/reload reads current folders, schema metadata and approved samples in a background job. Redmine startup does not run a scan.</p>
<%= button_to 'Refresh models', refresh_ai_models_path, method: :post %>
<%= button_to 'Test/reload sources', reload_ai_sources_path, method: :post %>
<% if @source_check['state'] %>
  <div class="box">
    <p><strong>Source check:</strong> <%= @source_check['state'].humanize %> <%= @source_check['checked_at'] %></p>
    <% if @source_check['error'] %><p class="error"><%= @source_check['error'] %></p><% end %>
    <table class="list"><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Result</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <% Array(@source_check['results']).each do |result| %>
        <tr><td><%= result['name'] %></td><td><%= result['status'] %></td><td><%= result['message'] %></td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody></table>
    <% if @source_check['state'] == 'queued' %><p>Refresh this page for completion. If it remains queued, check the job backend or run Test/reload again.</p><% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
<p>Enable the project module and grant enhancement plus ticket-edit permission. Source mappings grant those users access to retrieved content. Connection credentials are encrypted and never sent to OpenAI.</p>
<p>Only supported UTF-8 text/code files are scanned; binary/PDF/Word inputs need reviewed text exports. Optional database drivers must be available in Redmine's bundle.</p>
